# Committed on purpose, and load-bearing.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are INLINED BY NEXT.JS AT BUILD TIME — they are not
# read from the environment at runtime. Putting them only in wrangler.jsonc
# `vars` (which are runtime Worker env) is therefore not enough for anything the
# browser executes. RsvpVault shipped a bundle pointing at http://localhost:8080
# this way on 2026-07-27; SSR kept working, so the site looked healthy while
# every button was dead.
#
# MealMargin has no API, so today this file carries only the site URL (used for
# canonical/OG metadata). It exists anyway so the next person adding a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ value has somewhere obvious to put it instead of reaching for
# wrangler vars.
#
# These values are public by definition: they end up in a JavaScript bundle any
# visitor can read. Nothing secret belongs in this file.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://mealmargin.3pandalabs.com
